exercises.solution:
```python
def rot90(p):
    return (-p[1], p[0])

def reflect_x(p):
    return (p[0], -p[1])

def reflect_diag(p):
    return (p[1], p[0])

def then(f, g):
    return lambda p: g(f(p))
```

In `g(f(p))` the function `f` acts first, which is why mathematicians write the composite as $g \circ f$ (“$g$ after $f$”). With the order fixed, reflecting in the $x$-axis then in $y = x$ sends every grid point to its quarter-turn image; the reverse order sends $(1, 0)$ to $(0, -1)$, a quarter turn clockwise.
